:HELP NAME=ADDIMGCLGE.Add Image Catalog Entry (ADDIMGCLGE)
:P.Use the Add Image Catalog Entry (ADDIMGCLGE) command to add an image
to an image catalog&colon. a file in its directory, a file copied in, or
FROMFILE(*NEW) for a new volume.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDIMGCLGE/IMGCLG'.Image catalog (IMGCLG)
:P.The image catalog, which holds the image files of a virtual tape or
optical device.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDIMGCLGE/FROMDEV'.From optical device, or (FROMDEV)
:P.The device the data comes from.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDIMGCLGE/FROMFILE'.From image file (FROMFILE)
:P.The file the data comes from.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*NEW:EPK.
:PD.A new one.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDIMGCLGE/TOFILE'.To image file (TOFILE)
:P.The file that receives the data.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *FROMFILE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDIMGCLGE/IMGCLGIDX'.Image catalog index (IMGCLGIDX)
:P.The index of the image catalog entry.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*AVAIL:EPK.
:PD.Every available one.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 256.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDIMGCLGE/REPLACE'.Replace catalog entry (REPLACE)
:P.Whether an existing object of the same name is replaced. A replaced
object is moved to library QRPLOBJ when it is in use.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.An existing object of the same name is replaced.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.The command ends with a message when an object of the same name
exists.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDIMGCLGE/IMGSIZ'.Image size (IMGSIZ)
:P.The image size for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16000000.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CD650, *DVD2600, *DVD4700.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDIMGCLGE/VOLNAM'.Volume name (VOLNAM)
:P.The volume name for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*GEN:EPK.
:PD.Generated by the system.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDIMGCLGE/ALCSTG'.Allocate storage size (ALCSTG)
:P.The allocate storage size for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MIN:EPK.
:PD.The smallest value.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *IMGSIZ.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDIMGCLGE/WRTPTC'.Write protect (WRTPTC)
:P.Whether to write protect.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDIMGCLGE/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=ADDOPTCTG.Add Optical Cartridge (ADDOPTCTG)
:P.Use the Add Optical Cartridge (ADDOPTCTG) command to add an optical
cartridge to an optical media library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDOPTCTG/MLB'.Optical device (MLB)
:P.The optical device for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDOPTCTG/AUTL'.Authorization list (AUTL)
:P.The authorization list that secures the object.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*PRV:EPK.
:PD.The previous release.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. QOPTSEC.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDOPTCTG/DIR'.Rebuild directory index (DIR)
:P.Whether to rebuild directory index.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='ADDOPTCTG/MEDLOC'.Media location (MEDLOC)
:P.The media location for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *IOSTATION, *MAGAZINE.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHGIMGCLGE.Change Image Catalog Entry (CHGIMGCLGE)
:P.Use the Change Image Catalog Entry (CHGIMGCLGE) command to change an
image catalog entry's write protection or text.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGIMGCLGE/IMGCLG'.Image catalog (IMGCLG)
:P.The image catalog, which holds the image files of a virtual tape or
optical device.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGIMGCLGE/IMGCLGIDX'.Image catalog index (IMGCLGIDX)
:P.The index of the image catalog entry.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 256.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGIMGCLGE/WRTPTC'.Write protect (WRTPTC)
:P.The write protect for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The value does not change.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHGIMGCLGE/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The text does not change.
:PT.:PK.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CHKOPT.Check Optical (CHKOPT)
:P.Use the Check Optical (CHKOPT) command to read every file of an
optical volume to its end (a QS/400 command of its own).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKOPT/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CHKOPT/DEV'.Optical device (DEV)
:P.The optical device for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=CRTIMGCLG.Create Image Catalog (CRTIMGCLG)
:P.Use the Create Image Catalog (CRTIMGCLG) command to create an image
catalog over an IFS directory.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTIMGCLG/IMGCLG'.Image catalog (IMGCLG)
:P.The image catalog, which holds the image files of a virtual tape or
optical device.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTIMGCLG/DIR'.Directory (DIR)
:P.The directory for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTIMGCLG/TYPE'.Image catalog type (TYPE)
:P.The image catalog type for this command.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OPT, *TAP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTIMGCLG/CRTDIR'.Create directory (CRTDIR)
:P.Whether to create directory.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTIMGCLG/IMPORT'.Import image catalog (IMPORT)
:P.Whether to import image catalog.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTIMGCLG/CLGASPTHLD'.Catalog ASP threshold (CLGASPTHLD)
:P.The catalog ASP threshold for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTIMGCLG/ADDVRTVOL'.Add virtual volumes (ADDVRTVOL)
:P.The add virtual volumes for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PK.*DIR:EPK.
:PD.A directory.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 256.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTIMGCLG/IMGSIZ'.Image size (IMGSIZ)
:P.The image size for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 16000000.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *CD650, *DVD2600, *DVD4700.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTIMGCLG/REFIMGCLG'.Reference image catalog (REFIMGCLG)
:P.The reference image catalog for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTIMGCLG/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='CRTIMGCLG/AUT'.Authority (AUT)
:P.The authority the public (users with no private authority and no
group authority) gets to the new object.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*EXCLUDE:EPK.
:PD.No authority&colon. the object cannot be used.
:PT.:PK.*CHANGE:EPK.
:PD.Change authority&colon. all data authorities and operational
authority. The object can be used and its contents changed.
:PT.:PK.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All authority&colon. the user can do anything with the object except
change its owner or what secures it.
:PT.:PK.*USE:EPK.
:PD.Use authority&colon. the object can be read and run but not changed.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DLTIMGCLG.Delete Image Catalog (DLTIMGCLG)
:P.Use the Delete Image Catalog (DLTIMGCLG) command to delete an image
catalog; KEEP(*NO) deletes its images.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTIMGCLG/IMGCLG'.Image catalog (IMGCLG)
:P.The image catalog, which holds the image files of a virtual tape or
optical device.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DLTIMGCLG/KEEP'.Keep optical image files (KEEP)
:P.Whether to keep optical image files.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPOPT.Display Optical (DSPOPT)
:P.Use the Display Optical (DSPOPT) command to display an optical
volume's attributes, directories, files, or the saves on it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPOPT/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPOPT/DEV'.Optical device (DEV)
:P.The optical device for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPOPT/DATA'.Data type (DATA)
:P.The data type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*SAVRST:EPK.
:PD.Save and restore operations.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *VOLATR, *DIRATR, *FILATR.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPOPT/PATH'.Path (PATH)
:P.The path for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.path-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a path name of up to 1024 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.When no value is given, '/' is used.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPOPT/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:PT.:PK.*OUTFILE:EPK.
:PD.The output goes to the database file named by OUTFILE.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPOPT/OUTFILE'.File to receive output (OUTFILE)
:P.The database file that receives the output when OUTPUT(*OUTFILE) is
given. The file is created with the system's model format when it does
not exist.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Library&colon. the name can be qualified by it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.The library list of the job is searched; the first match is used.
:PT.:PK.*CURLIB:EPK.
:PD.The current library of the job. When the job has none, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DSPOPT/OUTMBR'.Output member options (OUTMBR)
:P.The member of the output file that receives the records, and whether
they replace the member's records or are added after them.
:P.The value has 2 parts, given in order&colon.
:H4.Part 1&colon. Member to receive output
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*FIRST:EPK.
:PD.The first member of the file. A member with the file's name is added
when the file has none.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:H4.Part 2&colon. Replace or add records
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*REPLACE:EPK.
:PD.The member's records are cleared first.
:PT.:PK.*ADD:EPK.
:PD.The records are added after the member's records.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DUPOPT.Duplicate Optical (DUPOPT)
:P.Use the Duplicate Optical (DUPOPT) command to copy one optical volume
onto another.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPOPT/FROMVOL'.From volume identifier (FROMVOL)
:P.The from volume identifier for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPOPT/TOVOL'.To volume identifier (TOVOL)
:P.The to volume identifier for this command.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPOPT/NEWVOL'.New volume identifier (NEWVOL)
:P.The new volume identifier for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *TOVOL, *FROMVOL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPOPT/CLEAR'.Clear (CLEAR)
:P.Whether to clear.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPOPT/FROMDEV'.From device (FROMDEV)
:P.The device the data comes from.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPOPT/TODEV'.To device (TODEV)
:P.The device the data goes to.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPOPT/ALWMEDERR'.Allow media errors (ALWMEDERR)
:P.The allow media errors for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 1000000.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPOPT/FROMENDOPT'.From end of media option (FROMENDOPT)
:P.The from end of media option for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is when the operation ends; the next
operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded when the operation ends.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='DUPOPT/TOENDOPT'.To end of media option (TOENDOPT)
:P.What the to-device does with the tape when the operation ends.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is when the operation ends; the next
operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded when the operation ends.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=INZOPT.Initialize Optical (INZOPT)
:P.Use the Initialize Optical (INZOPT) command to initialize an optical
volume.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZOPT/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*MOUNTED:EPK.
:PD.Whatever volume is in the device.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZOPT/NEWVOL'.New volume identifier (NEWVOL)
:P.The new volume identifier for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *VOL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZOPT/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZOPT/THRESHOLD'.Volume full threshold (THRESHOLD)
:P.The volume full threshold for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 99.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZOPT/CHECK'.Check for an active volume (CHECK)
:P.Whether to check for an active volume.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZOPT/ENDOPT'.End of media option (ENDOPT)
:P.What the device does with the tape when the operation ends&colon.
leave it where it is, rewind it, or rewind and unload it.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LEAVE:EPK.
:PD.The tape stays where it is; the next operation goes on from there.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZOPT/CLEAR'.Clear (CLEAR)
:P.Whether to clear.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZOPT/TEXT'.Text 'description' (TEXT)
:P.A short description of the object, up to 50 characters, shown by the
work-with and display commands next to its name.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*BLANK:EPK.
:PD.No text.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 50 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZOPT/TYPE'.Volume type (TYPE)
:P.The volume type for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *PRIMARY, *BACKUP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZOPT/CCSID'.Coded character set ID (CCSID)
:P.The coded character set identifier&colon. the code page and character
set the data is in, or is to be converted to.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*CALC:EPK.
:PD.The system calculates the value.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='INZOPT/MEDFMT'.Media format (MEDFMT)
:P.The media format for this command.
:P.The prompt shows this parameter after F10 (Additional parameters).
:P.Also accepted&colon. *MEDTYPE, *UDF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=LODIMGCLG.Load or Unload Image Catalog (LODIMGCLG)
:P.Use the Load or Unload Image Catalog (LODIMGCLG) command to load an
image catalog on a virtual device, or unload it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LODIMGCLG/IMGCLG'.Image catalog (IMGCLG)
:P.The image catalog, which holds the image files of a virtual tape or
optical device.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LODIMGCLG/OPTION'.Option (OPTION)
:P.The option for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded when the operation ends.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LOAD, *MOUNT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LODIMGCLG/DEV'.Device (DEV)
:P.The device for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=LODIMGCLGE.Load/Unload Image Catalog Entry (LODIMGCLGE)
:P.Use the Load/Unload Image Catalog Entry (LODIMGCLGE) command to load,
unload or mount one image catalog entry.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LODIMGCLGE/IMGCLG'.Image catalog (IMGCLG)
:P.The image catalog, which holds the image files of a virtual tape or
optical device.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LODIMGCLGE/IMGCLGIDX'.Image catalog index (IMGCLGIDX)
:P.The index of the image catalog entry.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 256.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LODIMGCLGE/OPTION'.Option (OPTION)
:P.The option for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*UNLOAD:EPK.
:PD.The tape is rewound and unloaded when the operation ends.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *LOAD, *MOUNT.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=RMVIMGCLGE.Remove Image Catalog Entry (RMVIMGCLGE)
:P.Use the Remove Image Catalog Entry (RMVIMGCLGE) command to remove an
entry from an image catalog.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVIMGCLGE/IMGCLG'.Image catalog (IMGCLG)
:P.The image catalog, which holds the image files of a virtual tape or
optical device.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVIMGCLGE/IMGCLGIDX'.Image catalog index (IMGCLGIDX)
:P.The index of the image catalog entry.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.number:EPV.
:PD.Type a whole number. The value must be from 1 to 256.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *VOL.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVIMGCLGE/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 32 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='RMVIMGCLGE/KEEP'.Keep image file (KEEP)
:P.Whether to keep image file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=VFYIMGCLG.Verify Image Catalog (VFYIMGCLG)
:P.Use the Verify Image Catalog (VFYIMGCLG) command to verify that an
image catalog's images are there and, for the install types, form one
ordered set.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='VFYIMGCLG/IMGCLG'.Image catalog (IMGCLG)
:P.The image catalog, which holds the image files of a virtual tape or
optical device.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='VFYIMGCLG/TYPE'.Verify type (TYPE)
:P.The verify type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*OTHER:EPK.
:PD.Other.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *UPGRADE, *LIC, *PTF.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='VFYIMGCLG/SORT'.Sort image catalog (SORT)
:P.Whether to sort image catalog.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='VFYIMGCLG/NFSSHR'.Network file server share (NFSSHR)
:P.Whether to network file server share.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='VFYIMGCLG/LNG'.Language (LNG)
:P.The language feature of the licensed program.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*DFT:EPK.
:PD.The default value.
:PT.:PV.character-value:EPV.
:PD.Type up to 4 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKIMGCLG.Work with Image Catalogs (WRKIMGCLG)
:P.Use the Work with Image Catalogs (WRKIMGCLG) command to work with
image catalogs.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKIMGCLG/IMGCLG'.Image catalog (IMGCLG)
:P.The image catalog, which holds the image files of a virtual tape or
optical device.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKIMGCLG/TYPE'.Image catalog type (TYPE)
:P.The image catalog type for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:EPARML.
:P.Also accepted&colon. *OPT, *TAP.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKIMGCLGE.Work with Image Catalog Entries (WRKIMGCLGE)
:P.Use the Work with Image Catalog Entries (WRKIMGCLGE) command to work
with the entries of an image catalog.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKIMGCLGE/IMGCLG'.Image catalog (IMGCLG)
:P.The image catalog, which holds the image files of a virtual tape or
optical device.
:P.A value is required.
:PARML.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKIMGCLGE/OUTPUT'.Output (OUTPUT)
:P.Where the command sends what it produces&colon. to the display of an
interactive job, or to a spooled file of the job's printer file. Some
commands can also write it to a database file.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*:EPK.
:PD.The output is shown at the display of an interactive job, and
printed for a batch job.
:PT.:PK.*PRINT:EPK.
:PD.The output is printed with the job's spooled output.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=WRKOPTVOL.Work with Optical Volumes (WRKOPTVOL)
:P.Use the Work with Optical Volumes (WRKOPTVOL) command to work with
the optical volumes the system knows.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOPTVOL/DEV'.Optical device (DEV)
:P.The optical device for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOPTVOL/VOL'.Volume identifier (VOL)
:P.The volume identifier of the tape or optical volume. *MOUNTED uses
whatever volume is in the device.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PV.generic-name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 32 characters, or a generic name&colon.
characters that end with an asterisk (*) select every name that starts
with them.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOPTVOL/CSI'.Side information (CSI)
:P.The side information for this command.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*ALL:EPK.
:PD.All of them.
:PT.:PK.*NONE:EPK.
:PD.None.
:PT.:PV.name:EPV.
:PD.Type a name of up to 10 characters.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKOPTVOL/RTVEXTINFO'.Retrieve extended information (RTVEXTINFO)
:P.Whether to retrieve extended information.
:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*NO:EPK.
:PD.No.
:PT.:PK.*YES:EPK.
:PD.Yes.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
